@lingxinsuixing/dsh-agnes README · Tools：Every tool returns text: a path, a URL and a short summary. Nothing binary is put into the conversation.

Note on `size`: the API maps an exact size such as `1920x1080` to the nearest tier, so the `size` in the
result is the **real pixel size of the file on disk**, not necessarily what was asked for.

@lingxinsuixing/dsh-agnes README · Optional: image recognition：Image recognition is optional. Set `enableRecognition: false` in the plugin config and the
`agnes_image_recognize` tool is not registered at all — only image and video generation stay.
Tools are registered while the plugin loads, so switching it off takes effect after one DSH restart.

@lingxinsuixing/dsh-agnes README · Optional: image recognition：If your provider talks to Agnes over `api: openai-completions`, declare `reasoningEfforts` in the model entry as well.
Without it DSH does not send `reasoning_effort`, the gateway returns no `reasoning_content`, and the model writes its whole
reasoning process into the message body — the thinking chain ends up in the conversation.

@lingxinsuixing/dsh-agnes README · Where output goes：Generated media is written to the folder configured as `outputDir` (default: `media/` under the DSH home directory: `$DSH_HOME/media`, or `~/.dsh/media` when `$DSH_HOME` is not set). Each call returns the absolute path of the file it wrote.
You can also change it from the plugin page (plugin → this package → page → “Output folder and read scope”),
together with `allowedReadRoots` — the folders recognition is allowed to read from (empty = no restriction).

@lingxinsuixing/dsh-agnes README · Where output goes：Free models are available: the whole image model line is currently free, and the video line has a free tier
(`agnes-video-2.5-flash`, 720P only). Model list and prices: https://www.agnes-ai.cn/zh-Hans/docs/overview

A `saveTo` argument must point to an **existing** directory: the plugin never creates directories at arbitrary paths, and file names are generated by the plugin, so nothing of yours is overwritten.

@lingxinsuixing/dsh-agnes README · Requirements：- DeepSeek Harness with `@deepseek-ai/schemastery` `>=3.18.1`
- An Agnes API key
- Agnes image generation is currently free; video generation is billed by Agnes per generated second (the `-flash` variant is currently limited to 720P)
